      <span style="background: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12); color: #c084fc; border: 1px solid rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">SURCHARGE AVOIDANCE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Eliminating Hidden Surcharges &amp; Demanding Written Binding Contracts for Bike Transport from Pune</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you book a bike transport from Pune to Varanasi, the advertised base fare often hides a few hidden charges that can inflate the final bill on moving day. Transporters who are less than honest will tack on extra fees for floor elevation, long carries, or toll taxes without prior disclosure.</p>

<p>Floor elevation surcharges arise when the pickup or delivery site is on a higher floor that requires a lift or additional manpower. A dishonest operator will claim a premium after the move, arguing that the “elevator fee” was not included in the original quote.</p>
<p>Long‑carry charges apply when the bike must be carried over a distance that exceeds the normal loading zone—say, a long stretch of road or a bridge that requires a special permit. In such cases, the transporter will add a “long‑carry” fee only after the job is underway.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Toll taxes are another common loophole.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>While most states impose a toll on trucks crossing certain highways, the transporter may refuse to pay the toll in advance, instead billing the customer for the entire toll amount at the end of the trip.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Because tolls are unpredictable, this tactic leaves the customer exposed to sudden, unplanned expenses.</span></li></ul>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
